parameters.description:
A list of up to 50 features. The value must be in the following format:

- **functionName** (feature name): The name of the feature. For a list of configurable features, see [feature list](~~410622~~).

- **argName**: A configuration item for the feature specified by **functionName**. You can specify multiple configuration items.

- **argValue**: The value of the configuration item.

- **parentid** (rule condition ID, optional): You can create a rule condition by configuring the **condition** function of the rules engine. A rule condition filters user requests based on various parameters. After a rule condition is created, a corresponding [configid](~~388994~~) is generated. You can use this configid as the value of the `ParentId` parameter to reference the rule condition in other functions. This way, you can combine rule conditions with feature configurations to create more flexible configurations. For more information, see [Parameters for domain name configuration features](~~410622~~).

```
[
 {
   "functionArgs": [
    {
     "argName": "feature parameter A", 
     "argValue": "value of feature parameter A"
    }, 
  {
    "argName": "feature parameter B", 
    "argValue": "value of feature parameter B"
     }
 ], 
 "functionName": "feature name"
    }
]
```
